{#- Apps and products (REQ-011 as amended by A-01, A-02; plan D-07, D-14, D-15):
    one article.card.app.portfolio-entry per entry of src/_data/portfolio.json,
    in data order, on the balanced subgrid — theme caption | chip row | name |
    summary | action row. The theme caption has its own track (not the chip
    row): the founder-confirmed private label fills a three-column card's
    width on its own, so the chip row holds only the status chip and stays
    one line. Copy comes from strings.portfolio.<key>; the status label from
    strings.portfolioStatus and the theme caption from strings.themes. The
    name is plain text in every card. The action row is the same element in
    every card, div.app-actions, and it holds the card's only links, each an
    a.app-action. First the entry's url (url set, the card gets app-linked):
    "Repository ↗" when the url is the public repository on github.com,
    "Website ↗" when it is the public page of a product whose repository is
    private (nivå since si-gyc4), so the card never calls a private
    repository open — or p.app-private with the private note (url null, no
    link to the app). Then, beside it, "Article →" when the entry names the
    article about the app (`article`, the post's file name; founder request
    2026-09-23, si-3hpa): a page of this site, so → where the links that
    leave it wear ↗, to the article in the page's language, and only while
    that language's posts collection lists it — the postBySlug filter
    (eleventy.config.js) finds no draft in the production build and no
    article dated after today, so neither is linked. .portfolio-entry,
    .portfolio-name and .app-actions are the content gate's stable hooks. -#}
{%- set apps = strings[lang].apps -%}
{%- set posts = collections["posts_" + lang] -%}
<section id="apps" class="section section-alt" aria-labelledby="apps-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">{{ apps.eyebrow }}</p>
      <h2 id="apps-title">{{ apps.heading }}</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">{{ apps.lead }}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="app-grid">
      {%- for entry in portfolio %}
      {%- set copy = strings[lang].portfolio[entry.key] %}
      {%- set appArticle = posts | postBySlug(entry.article) %}
      <article class="card app portfolio-entry reveal{% if entry.url %} app-linked{% endif %}">
        <p class="app-theme">{{ strings[lang].themes[entry.theme].title }}</p>
        <div class="app-top">
          <span class="chip chip-{{ entry.status }}"><span class="chip-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ strings[lang].portfolioStatus[entry.status] }}</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="app-name portfolio-name">{{ copy.name }}</h3>
        <p class="app-text">{{ copy.summary }}</p>
        <div class="app-actions">
          {%- if entry.url %}
          <a class="app-action" href="{{ entry.url }}">{{ strings[lang].portfolio.repoLink if entry.url.startsWith("https://github.com/") else strings[lang].portfolio.siteLink }}<span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          {%- else %}
          <p class="app-private">{{ strings[lang].portfolio.privateNote }}</p>
          {%- endif %}
          {%- if appArticle %}
          <a class="app-action" href="{{ appArticle.url }}">{{ strings[lang].portfolio.articleLink }}<span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          {%- endif %}
        </div>
      </article>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
